@startuml UML-IMPORT-PIPELINE
title KnowledgeOS — Import Pipeline
caption Architecture V3.0

skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor User
participant "Import Engine" as ImportEngine
participant "Data Exchange / Import Protocol" as Protocol
participant "OCR Provider" as OCR
participant "UDM Processing" as UDM
participant "DPM Processing" as DPM
participant "Library Engine" as Library
participant "Job System" as Jobs
participant "Search Engine" as Search
participant "AI Engine" as AI

User -> ImportEngine : Select source for import
ImportEngine -> Protocol : Open and validate source
Protocol --> ImportEngine : Normalized source stream

alt OCR required
  ImportEngine -> OCR : Request OCR processing
  OCR --> ImportEngine : Recognized content and layout evidence
end

ImportEngine -> UDM : Build semantic and structural model
UDM --> ImportEngine : Validated UDM

ImportEngine -> DPM : Build presentation and layout model
DPM --> ImportEngine : Validated DPM

ImportEngine -> Library : Commit Knowledge Object, UDM, DPM and Assets
Library --> ImportEngine : Canonical commit confirmed

ImportEngine --> User : Basic document available

ImportEngine -> Jobs : Schedule derived processing

par Search indexing
  Jobs -> Search : Build lexical and structural indexes
else Embeddings / semantic enrichment
  Jobs -> AI : Generate optional embeddings or AI-derived metadata
else Additional reconstruction
  Jobs -> DPM : Generate previews or derived presentation artifacts
end

note over ImportEngine, Library
  Canonical availability does not wait for every derived job.
end note

note over Jobs, AI
  Derived work is rebuildable and must not redefine canonical meaning silently.
end note

footer KnowledgeOS Architecture | UML | Version 3.0
@enduml
